prompt:
A knowledge graph was built from Wikipedia passages. A question has a gold answer. Below are graph nodes whose names occur in the gold answer (candidates).
Keep a candidate ONLY if the gold answer gives that entity AS the thing the question asks for (the answer itself, or one item of a list answer). Drop a candidate that is only context, a definition, a generic word (for example "theory", "class", "data") or part of how the answer is explained. Use only the question and the gold answer. Keep none if no candidate is the answer.
Return ONLY JSON: {"keep":[candidate names exactly as written],"reason":str (max 20 words)}
